  "id": "USN-8733-2",
  "summary": "gzip vulnerabilities",
  "details": "USN-8733-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Gzip. This update provides the\ncorresponding fix for Gzip on Ubuntu 14.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS and Ubuntu\n20.04 LTS.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\n Micha\u0142 Majchrowicz and Marcin Wyczechowski discovered that Gzip's gzexe\nutility created temporary files in an insecure manner when mktemp was\nunavailable. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to overwrite\narbitrary files. (CVE-2026-41991)\n\n Elias Hasas, Micha\u0142 Majchrowicz and Marcin Wyczechowski discovered that\nGzip incorrectly handled certain compressed files. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information or cause Gzip to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-41992)",
